WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.634
 Are you ready?

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.435
 Yes, I am.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.505
[music playing]

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:06.672
 It will--

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.741
[metal clangs]

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.645
WIL WILLIS: The Zande spear.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.214
 Ooh, boy!

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.949
WIL WILLIS (VOICEOVER): One
of the deadliest weapons used

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.050
by the Zande tribes
of Central Africa,

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.153
the Zande spear was
used for fighting as

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.487
well as for hunting.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.622
Known throughout history
as conquering warriors,

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.093
the Zande exhibited unmatched
skills on the battlefield.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.162
Affixed to a wooden
shaft, the spear

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:32.165
was suitable for throwing and
attacking from long distances.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.499
But its thrusting
ability made it

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.535
just as effective as
a close-combat weapon.

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:38.972
The sharp upper and lower
tines and multiple spikes

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.841
inflicted deadly wounds,
both upon entry and exit

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.309
from the victim's body.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.311
The Zande's lethal
use of the spear

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:49.381
can be seen highlighted in
the game "Deadliest Warrior."

00:00:49.481 --> 00:00:51.550
 Bladesmiths, I will
take your Zande spear

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.753
and deliver killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:55.755
Drew, you're up first.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.989
You ready?

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.457
 Let's make those
intestines out-testines.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:00:59.158
 All right.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.092
[laughs] Let's do that.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.195
I like that.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.497
DREW (VOICEOVER): Right now,
I'm about to hear Doug say,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.598
"It will kill."

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:09.135
And that's the only
thing I'm here for.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.238
 To help me out today, please
welcome back RJ Marcaida.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.707
He will have the pleasure of
wielding your Zande spear.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:18.311
[music playing]

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.629
[laughter]

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:39.799
All right, Drew.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:41.701
It feels very good in the hand.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.235
It lacerates deep.

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:45.371
When we thrust this into the
chest cavity, into the heart,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:49.141
on its way out, not only does
it take some skin with it,

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.477
but it also took out some ribs.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.247
Your tines right here from
the side entry, the spear

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.548
went all the way through.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.650
And on its way out,
it took everything

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.118
that was in its path.

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:00.653
But there is one issue.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.690
As you can see, your tip
right here broke off.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:08.727
But other than that, this
is a weapon that is deadly,

00:02:08.827 --> 00:02:10.162
and it will KEAL.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.530
 Thank you.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.099
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Jason, your turn.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.900
You ready?

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:14.633
 I know it'll cut.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.468
[laughs]

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:19.672
[music playing]

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.557
 All right, Jason.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.592
The balance of your
weapon feels good.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.762
When it penetrated into the
chest cavity, it hit a rib

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.397
and broke it in half.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:48.267
Got into the heart, and there
was no edge damage on your tip.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.936
All these hooks
right here did what

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.570
it's supposed to do--
into the abdomen,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.506
ripped everything
out, even the barb.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:57.410
And the beautiful thing
about this is it will KEAL.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.947
 That's what I wanted to hear.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.815
 Say hello to my
little friend here.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.286
Today, we're going to
test the overall strength

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:09.622
and construction of
your Zande spears by--

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.924
well, we're going to fire
them out of this cannon

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.926
into this wood block wall.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.094
Now, I'm not
concerned about what

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.529
your spears do to the wall.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.465
I want to see how well your
spears survive the wall.

00:03:19.531 --> 00:03:20.967
Drew, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.100
 No.
[laughs]

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.269
 Well, we're
gonna do it anyway.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.504
 Let's do it.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.941
[music playing]

00:03:40.485 --> 00:03:41.988
 That worked really well, Drew.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.690
Despite the fact that you did
lose a little bit of your tip

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.526
in the kill test, it
didn't have any effect

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.462
going into that block wall.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.899
Matter of fact, you sunk
all the way down here.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.233
Very impressive.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.301
Your shaft is fine.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.168
Nothing loosened up.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.203
Nothing cracked.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.705
Your spearhead is still solid.

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.475
Overall, it survived.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.041
Very good.

00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:04.409
 Thank you.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.145
 So, Jason, what
are you thinking?

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.180
 Thinking let's make splinters.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:11.718
[music playing]

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.288
 That's a problem.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.522
 Oh, God, no.

00:04:19.424 --> 00:04:21.995
I'm seeing it hang up
a bit on the barrel,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.597
and my heart just
absolutely sinks.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.873
 Jason, we've got
a big problem here.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.975
The parameters that we
set for these weapons

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.543
are for testing purposes.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.313
Because your blade didn't meet
the inch and a half parameter

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:43.348
with a circular
cross-section, we cannot fit

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:46.118
the shaft of your
weapon down the barrel

00:04:46.184 --> 00:04:47.853
of our testing apparatus here.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.523
And because we can't
test it evenly and fairly

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.926
with Drew's blade, I have to ask
you to please leave the forge.

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:59.432
 This was absolutely
worst-case scenario.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.901
I'm proud that I got
this far, but I'm

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.370
incredibly disappointed.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.706
 Well, Drew, in a competition
where attention to detail

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.341
is just as critical
as craftsmanship,

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.510
you are the Forged
in Fire Champion

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.946
and will be collecting
a check for $10,000.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:14.680
Good job.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.714
[applause]

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.817
 Oh, my god.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:18.617
Oh!

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.720
 How you feeling right now?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.323
 I'm 18 years old, and I'm
the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:25.824
What-- what just happened?

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.127
 Well, I think the best
blade just won, my friend.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.295
Come over here and
shake our hand.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.397
 Oh, god.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.133
Didn't want to win
this way, but I won.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.069
And that's kind of
all that matters.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:39.705
I started bladesmithing
seriously because of this show.

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:43.743
I learned all that I had
to learn to make it here.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.077
And I just won.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.747
This-- this is the dream.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.281
Oh, my god, man!

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:52.885
[music playing]

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.027
WIL WILLIS: Black
Beard's infamous cutlass.

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:08.601
Among the most notorious
pirates of the 18th century,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.903
Blackbeard terrorized
Caribbean and Atlantic

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:13.573
merchant shipping with his
trademark cutlass in hand.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.375
Its short but thick curved blade
featured a razor-sharp edge

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.910
that was ideal for
hacking and slashing

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.013
during close-quarters combat
while seizing small vessels.

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:24.716
In his legendary battle with
Captain Robert Maynard in 1718,

00:06:24.816 --> 00:06:26.518
Blackbeard's cutlass
broke Maynard's sword

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:28.821
in half with a single blow.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.324
Today, Blackbeard's
menacing presence and expert

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.993
swordsmanship can still
be seen in the video game

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.294
"Assassin's Creed IV--

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:36.762
Black Flag."

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:39.731
 Bladesmiths, to test the
lethality of your cutlass,

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:41.267
I'm going to inflict
lethal wounds

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.335
on these ballistic dummies.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:44.169
Jason, you're up first.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:45.103
You ready?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.072
 I sure hope so, Doug.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.307
 Let's do this.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:51.944
[music playing]

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:10.630
 [chuckling]

00:07:13.398 --> 00:07:14.667
 All right, Jason.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.036
You got a very big
handle here, but at least

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.371
it's got the swells.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:19.672
It's got an indexing to
when I hold on to it,

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.307
I can tell where the edge is.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:24.710
The weight that you have in this
weapon is so light in the sense

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.945
that I can wield it
even around here.

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:30.048
You cut the clavicle into
the ribs, all the way

00:07:30.148 --> 00:07:31.550
through the lungs.

00:07:31.616 --> 00:07:35.220
And, definitely, it will KEAL.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.755
 All I ever wanted to hear.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:37.756
Made my day.

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:38.957
DOUG MARCAIDA: Seth,
you're up next.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:39.692
You ready?

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.526
 Get some.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:44.197
[music playing]

00:08:14.593 --> 00:08:16.095
 All right, Seth.

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:18.864
Your sword is forward-heavy
without a balance coming back.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.900
I don't know whose shoulder's
going to hurt more,

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.334
the dummy's or mine.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.137
But your weapon, sir, will KEAL.

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:26.038
 Thank you.

00:08:29.107 --> 00:08:32.178
 To test the strength and
durability of your swords,

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.812
I'll be chopping
through these bones

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:35.748
and then attacking that peg leg.

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:38.985
Now, remember, this test is
not about what your blades

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:40.219
do to these targets.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.821
It's about what these
targets do to your blades.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.156
Jason, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:44.890
 Nope.

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:45.591
 [laughs]

00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:48.760
[music playing]

00:08:48.827 --> 00:08:50.196
 [sighs]

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:17.356
 The balance of your
weapon is really nice,

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:19.358
which is surprising
because you've made

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.794
a two-handed cutlass.

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:25.564
Your blade held up very well,
except for the one little chip.

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:26.465
And it's not even a chip.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:27.499
It's a roll.

00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:29.001
So it didn't blow out.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:30.168
It's a good job.

00:09:30.268 --> 00:09:31.203
 Thank you, Dave.

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:31.970
DAVID BAKER: All right, Seth.

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:32.805
Are you ready?

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:33.372
 Yes, sir.

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:36.842
[music playing]

00:09:56.695 --> 00:09:57.897
 All right, Seth.

00:09:57.963 --> 00:10:01.100
First up, this thing's a beast.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.738
It is probably a pound heavier
than your competitor's sword.

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:09.541
Your blade-- I mean, I can
run my fingernail down this.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:11.943
I can see a couple
of glinting spots,

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:13.846
but it really didn't
take any damage.

00:10:16.748 --> 00:10:17.916
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:20.052
Let's find out if
there's any edge left.

00:10:20.118 --> 00:10:23.189
This is the rope cut
and pirate sail slash.

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:24.789
To test the edge
of your cutlass,

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.459
I will cut this rope,
which will raise the sail,

00:10:27.525 --> 00:10:29.895
and then I will slash the sail.

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:32.398
This is all about
what your sword

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:34.733
will do to the sail and rope.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:35.768
Jason, you're up first.

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:36.335
Ready?

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:37.302
 Yes, sir.

00:10:37.403 --> 00:10:40.906
[music playing]

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:56.789
 Arr-righty, Jason.

00:10:56.855 --> 00:10:59.125
Your edge cut through
the rope easily,

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:02.094
and cuts with every
part that the edge

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.530
met on this pirate sail.

00:11:04.597 --> 00:11:08.300
Overall, sir, your
sword will cut.

00:11:08.367 --> 00:11:09.568
 Awesome.

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:10.502
DOUG MARCAIDA: Seth,
how are you feeling?

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:11.303
 Feeling good.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.070
Let's go.

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:12.705
 Let's do this.

00:11:12.772 --> 00:11:16.342
[music playing]

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:39.899
All right, Seth.

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:41.934
What are the chances you
find a very dull spot

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.502
on the first cut on the rope?

00:11:43.602 --> 00:11:46.939
But on the second cut, I had
found our spot that was sharp.

00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:50.642
But on the sail, working
a heavy sword like this

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:51.844
affects my cuts.

00:11:56.082 --> 00:11:59.518
 Jason, Seth, the judges
have tested your weapons,

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:01.454
and they've made
a final decision.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.322
The new Forged in
Fire Champion is--

00:12:07.092 --> 00:12:08.393
Jason.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.296
Congratulations, you're the
new Forged in Fire Champion.

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:14.499
Seth, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:17.536
Please surrender your blade.

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:18.870
Jason, congratulations.

00:12:18.937 --> 00:12:21.006
You "arrr" our new
Forged in Fire Champion,

00:12:21.072 --> 00:12:23.441
and that's a title that comes
with a bundle of bullion

00:12:23.508 --> 00:12:25.344
that's worth 10 grand.

00:12:25.444 --> 00:12:26.612
How you feeling right now?

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:29.615
 [laughs] I mean, come on.

00:12:29.681 --> 00:12:30.482
That's incredible.

00:12:30.582 --> 00:12:31.784
Forged in Fire Champion?

00:12:31.851 --> 00:12:35.421
[music playing]

00:12:40.792 --> 00:12:41.727
WIL WILLIS: The spiked shield.

00:12:41.794 --> 00:12:44.429
 Oh, [bleep].

00:12:44.496 --> 00:12:46.498
WIL WILLIS (VOICEOVER): Dating
back to prehistoric times,

00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:49.335
the shield is the oldest
form of protection, designed

00:12:49.401 --> 00:12:51.736
to block attacks from
weapons like spears,

00:12:51.803 --> 00:12:54.473
swords, axes, or arrows.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.941
Over time, they
have varied greatly

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:58.244
in size and construction,
using material

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:02.781
such as steel, wood, animal
hide, and even turtle shells.

00:13:02.847 --> 00:13:04.983
Used primarily as
a defense weapon,

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.553
the shield can also be used to
attack by punching an opponent

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.855
with either its face or rim.

00:13:10.922 --> 00:13:13.091
Sometime around the
Middle Ages, spikes

00:13:13.158 --> 00:13:16.461
were incorporated, adding
an extra level of brutality

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:17.629
to its design.

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:19.198
The long steel
spike could deliver

00:13:19.264 --> 00:13:21.733
deadly blows,
oftentimes immediately

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.702
disemboweling the attacker.

00:13:23.802 --> 00:13:25.938
The most notable
spiked shields today

00:13:26.005 --> 00:13:30.509
can be seen in the popular
video game series "Skyrim."

00:13:30.576 --> 00:13:33.812
 Gentlemen, between the
13th and the 16th century,

00:13:33.879 --> 00:13:35.480
spiked shields
were commonly used

00:13:35.547 --> 00:13:39.785
by infantry to protect from
swords, spears, and arrows.

00:13:39.885 --> 00:13:41.853
I'm going to fire three
bolts from a crossbow

00:13:41.953 --> 00:13:43.522
to test each of your shields.

00:13:43.589 --> 00:13:47.126
If your shield is strong,
it should deflect the arrow.

00:13:47.193 --> 00:13:48.260
Ilya, you're up.

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.261
You ready?

00:13:49.361 --> 00:13:50.228
 Yes, I am.

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:53.899
[music playing]

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:15.954
 I can see where
the bolts hit, Ilya.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:20.359
Small impact there,
here, and right there.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:23.595
Nothing that would even threaten
the man behind this shield, so

00:14:23.695 --> 00:14:25.731
that's very well done.

00:14:25.831 --> 00:14:27.099
Michael, you're up.

00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:27.899
You ready?

00:14:27.999 --> 00:14:28.833
 I think so.
Let's do this.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:29.568
DAVID BAKER: All right.

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:33.072
[music playing]

00:14:41.713 --> 00:14:43.048
 Yes.

00:14:43.115 --> 00:14:45.016
 Well, Michael, I
can see where one hit.

00:14:45.116 --> 00:14:47.085
You have a bit of a dimple.

00:14:47.185 --> 00:14:49.054
One impacted somewhere
on the center bust.

00:14:49.154 --> 00:14:51.190
You could actually hear it.

00:14:51.257 --> 00:14:52.891
[metal thudding]

00:14:52.958 --> 00:14:54.626
And though there are
some cosmetic issues

00:14:54.693 --> 00:14:58.530
with your shield, it certainly
held up to the strength test.

00:14:58.597 --> 00:14:59.331
So, well done.

00:14:59.431 --> 00:15:00.532
 Thank you.

00:15:00.598 --> 00:15:01.767
DAVID BAKER: Doug?

00:15:01.833 --> 00:15:03.902
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:15:03.969 --> 00:15:06.071
With your shield, I
will take four hits

00:15:06.138 --> 00:15:08.674
on this ballistics dummy
that's wearing chainmail.

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:09.875
Ilya, you're up.

00:15:09.942 --> 00:15:10.708
Are you ready?

00:15:10.775 --> 00:15:12.811
 Yes, I am.

00:15:12.878 --> 00:15:16.382
[music playing]

00:15:23.988 --> 00:15:25.790
 The shield feels
good in the hand.

00:15:25.857 --> 00:15:27.626
I can maneuver in
different ways, not only

00:15:27.692 --> 00:15:31.864
to protect, but also to attack.

00:15:31.964 --> 00:15:33.599
Now, let's see how
much damage it did.

00:15:36.067 --> 00:15:38.670
The killing blows
were right here, where

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.138
it penetrated all the way.

00:15:40.205 --> 00:15:43.409
That's to the sternum
and into the lung.

00:15:43.509 --> 00:15:47.045
In-- that is in the belly.

00:15:47.146 --> 00:15:53.018
That goes all the way into
this ballistics dummy.

00:15:53.085 --> 00:15:58.557
Your shield and the
spike will KEAL.

00:15:58.657 --> 00:15:59.391
Mike, it's your turn.

00:15:59.458 --> 00:15:59.925
You ready?

00:16:00.025 --> 00:16:01.226
 All right.

00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:03.261
 Mike, your spike's
a little bit loose.

00:16:03.362 --> 00:16:05.230
Let's see how it
goes in the test.

00:16:05.297 --> 00:16:06.497
 We'll see.

00:16:06.598 --> 00:16:10.102
[music playing]

00:16:13.005 --> 00:16:15.040
Oh-ho-ho.

00:16:15.107 --> 00:16:17.209
 Mike, it feels
good in the hand.

00:16:17.275 --> 00:16:19.277
You can strike with the edges.

00:16:19.377 --> 00:16:22.648
You can accompany it
with the other hand.

00:16:22.715 --> 00:16:24.583
It moves well.

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:26.151
The spike did hold up.

00:16:26.218 --> 00:16:27.652
Now, let's see how
much damage we did.

00:16:27.719 --> 00:16:28.487
 All right.

00:16:33.192 --> 00:16:34.359
God.

00:16:34.459 --> 00:16:36.895
 Your spike definitely
penetrated on both punctures.

00:16:36.962 --> 00:16:38.397
Right here probably
where the diaphragm

00:16:38.464 --> 00:16:43.001
is, and in the abdomen right
here, all the way through.

00:16:43.101 --> 00:16:46.671
Your shield will KEAL.

00:16:46.738 --> 00:16:47.906
 Thank you.

00:16:48.006 --> 00:16:49.641
 Bladesmiths, this
is the sharpness test.

00:16:49.741 --> 00:16:51.977
I will attach your shield
to this mechanical device.

00:16:52.077 --> 00:16:53.745
I will then release your
shield to see if it'll

00:16:53.845 --> 00:16:55.113
puncture the steel drum.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.315
If your spike is sharp,
it should go in easily.

00:16:57.382 --> 00:17:00.319
If not, well, it may
just dent the drum.

00:17:00.386 --> 00:17:00.852
Ilya, you're up.

00:17:00.919 --> 00:17:01.653
Are you ready?

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:02.654
 Yes, I am.

00:17:02.721 --> 00:17:04.256
 3, 2, 1.

00:17:04.323 --> 00:17:05.090
Engaging.

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:13.698
Well, Ilya, your spike went
cleanly through the drum

00:17:13.765 --> 00:17:15.267
and all the way out.

00:17:15.333 --> 00:17:18.970
I don't see any problems or
any deformations on your spike.

00:17:19.037 --> 00:17:20.339
So it held up very well.

00:17:20.439 --> 00:17:20.939
Good job.

00:17:21.039 --> 00:17:22.206
 Thank you.

00:17:22.307 --> 00:17:23.541
 Mike, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:17:23.608 --> 00:17:24.309
 Oh, yeah.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.011
Let's do this.

00:17:26.078 --> 00:17:27.746
 And in 3, 2, 1.

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:28.580
Engaging.

00:17:33.418 --> 00:17:35.087
 Phew.

00:17:35.154 --> 00:17:38.523
 Well, Mike, your spike
went all the way through.

00:17:38.623 --> 00:17:39.658
Got stuck a little bit.

00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:41.125
It came out cleanly.

00:17:41.225 --> 00:17:44.696
But I do not see any
damage to your spike.

00:17:44.763 --> 00:17:45.563
Good job, sir.

00:17:45.663 --> 00:17:46.932
 Thank you.

00:17:46.998 --> 00:17:49.134
 The judges have
scrutinized your work,

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.336
and they've made a final
decision about which of you is

00:17:51.402 --> 00:17:53.271
the Forged in Fire
Champion, who will

00:17:53.338 --> 00:17:56.608
receive a check for $10,000.

00:17:56.675 --> 00:18:00.878
Ilya-- you are the
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:03.549
[music playing]

00:18:03.615 --> 00:18:04.615
 Congratulations.

00:18:04.682 --> 00:18:05.851
 Thank you.

00:18:05.951 --> 00:18:08.654
 Mike, your shield
did not make the cut.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.089
Please surrender your shield.

00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:13.659
 Thank you, gentlemen.

00:18:13.725 --> 00:18:14.993
This was a fantastic experience.

00:18:15.059 --> 00:18:16.494
I think I performed very well.

00:18:16.561 --> 00:18:18.196
So as much as I would
have liked to win,

00:18:18.262 --> 00:18:21.533
this still feels like a victory.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.034
 Ilya, congratulations.

00:18:23.101 --> 00:18:24.302
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion

00:18:24.402 --> 00:18:26.938
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:18:27.038 --> 00:18:28.139
[applause]

00:18:28.206 --> 00:18:30.108
 Thank you.

00:18:30.175 --> 00:18:31.576
 The way that all
works together--

00:18:31.676 --> 00:18:34.479
I mean, just fantastic
piece, I think.

00:18:34.545 --> 00:18:37.249
 I'm fairly satisfied
with the end result.

00:18:37.315 --> 00:18:43.322
I might not often show it,
but trust me, I am proud.

00:18:43.422 --> 00:18:46.191
The prize money is
already pretty much spent

00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:48.360
on student loans
and my girlfriend's

00:18:48.427 --> 00:18:50.662
education in astrophysics.

00:18:50.729 --> 00:18:55.901
I'm the Forged in Fire Champion,
and it feels pretty good.

00:18:55.968 --> 00:18:59.471
[music playing]

00:19:03.408 --> 00:19:04.743
WIL WILLIS: The
Landsknecht sword.

00:19:09.347 --> 00:19:12.417
Created by Emperor Maximilian
I in the 15th century,

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:14.686
the Landsknecht were a
deadly mercenary force

00:19:14.753 --> 00:19:17.488
armed with pikes,
swords, and crossbows.

00:19:17.555 --> 00:19:19.158
The most battle-proven
Landsknecht

00:19:19.258 --> 00:19:22.394
mercenaries were armed with
massive two-handed swords.

00:19:22.494 --> 00:19:25.730
These imposing blades featured
parrying lugs above the guard

00:19:25.797 --> 00:19:27.566
to deflect enemy attacks.

00:19:27.666 --> 00:19:29.534
Earning double the
pay of their peers,

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.037
these garishly dressed
swordsmen of fortune

00:19:32.104 --> 00:19:34.439
would rush headlong into
enemy pikes in an effort

00:19:34.505 --> 00:19:36.908
to disrupt their
opponent's formations.

00:19:36.975 --> 00:19:38.409
Today, you can see
the Landsknecht

00:19:38.476 --> 00:19:41.246
sword in the hit mobile
strategy game "DomiNations."

00:19:41.312 --> 00:19:42.981
 Bladesmiths, the
two-handed German

00:19:43.048 --> 00:19:48.085
Landsknecht sword's a big sword,
so we're expecting big damage.

00:19:48.186 --> 00:19:49.588
I will take your
sword and deliver

00:19:49.655 --> 00:19:53.992
slashes, thrusts, and chops
on this wild boar carcass.

00:19:54.059 --> 00:19:54.826
Todd, you're up first.

00:19:54.893 --> 00:19:55.593
You ready?

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:56.127
 Yes, I am.

00:19:56.228 --> 00:19:56.895
 Let's do this.

00:19:56.962 --> 00:20:00.532
[music playing]

00:20:24.823 --> 00:20:25.891
All right, Todd.

00:20:25.991 --> 00:20:27.926
First up, your
handle construction.

00:20:27.992 --> 00:20:30.195
It's comfortable to hold on to.

00:20:30.262 --> 00:20:33.865
You have a very thick
and wide and stout edge,

00:20:33.931 --> 00:20:35.833
so it's a chopper, not a slicer.

00:20:35.933 --> 00:20:40.305
The big issue I have with this
is that it's a heavy sword.

00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:43.808
But despite its
weight, it will KEAL.

00:20:43.875 --> 00:20:44.810
 Yes.

00:20:44.876 --> 00:20:45.944
 All right, DJ, it's your turn.

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:46.744
You ready?

00:20:46.811 --> 00:20:47.546
 Yeah.

00:20:47.613 --> 00:20:51.016
[music playing]

00:21:15.206 --> 00:21:17.308
 DJ, let's talk
about your sword here.

00:21:17.408 --> 00:21:19.443
It's even heavier
than the other sword.

00:21:19.544 --> 00:21:22.013
The tip you have
over here is wide.

00:21:22.113 --> 00:21:23.281
The first thrust went in.

00:21:23.347 --> 00:21:25.784
The second one
couldn't, and I tried.

00:21:28.753 --> 00:21:31.956
The one thing it did
was break its back.

00:21:32.056 --> 00:21:36.794
A thrust like that, and a broken
back like that, will KEAL.

00:21:36.894 --> 00:21:37.696
 All right.

00:21:41.032 --> 00:21:42.901
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:21:43.001 --> 00:21:45.570
And to test the overall
construction of your blade,

00:21:45.637 --> 00:21:48.907
I'll be both stabbing and
chopping into this steel plate.

00:21:48.974 --> 00:21:49.975
All right, Todd,
you're up first.

00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:50.875
Are you ready?

00:21:50.942 --> 00:21:51.576
 Yes.

00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:54.913
[music playing]

00:22:21.305 --> 00:22:22.240
 All right, Todd.

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:25.310
You took some pretty good rolls.

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:28.980
These rolls are fairly
deep, but it held up.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:30.882
Nicely done.

00:22:30.949 --> 00:22:31.816
All right, DJ.

00:22:31.883 --> 00:22:32.884
You ready for this?

00:22:32.984 --> 00:22:34.252
 Yeah.

00:22:34.319 --> 00:22:35.853
[music playing]

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:37.789
Oh, Lord.

00:22:37.856 --> 00:22:41.460
[music playing]

00:23:03.014 --> 00:23:04.215
 All right, DJ.

00:23:04.282 --> 00:23:07.418
This weapon is heavy.

00:23:07.518 --> 00:23:08.453
Look at that balance point.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:09.955
It's so far forward.

00:23:10.021 --> 00:23:13.191
Keeping that tip up is brutal.

00:23:13.291 --> 00:23:15.660
You've got a really,
really super stout edge,

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:18.863
and, honestly, it
held up quite well.

00:23:18.963 --> 00:23:21.967
There are some rolls
here where it connected,

00:23:22.033 --> 00:23:25.470
but the weapon's still solid.

00:23:25.537 --> 00:23:27.204
It's a strong blade.

00:23:27.271 --> 00:23:28.773
 Thank you.

00:23:28.839 --> 00:23:31.576
 All right, gentlemen, your
blades are still in one piece.

00:23:31.642 --> 00:23:33.478
Now let's see if they
still have an edge.

00:23:33.544 --> 00:23:36.213
To test that edge, I'll be
cutting through this cane.

00:23:36.314 --> 00:23:36.981
Todd, you're up.

00:23:37.048 --> 00:23:37.848
Are you ready?

00:23:37.915 --> 00:23:38.349
 Yes.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:39.350
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:43.021
[music playing]

00:23:57.202 --> 00:24:00.772
[sword humming]

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:03.007
Hear that?

00:24:03.074 --> 00:24:04.142
 It sings.

00:24:04.209 --> 00:24:06.978
 It's like a tuning fork.

00:24:07.045 --> 00:24:09.681
All right, Todd, so let's talk
about your singing sword here.

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:13.117
[laughs] You definitely
have a sharp edge here.

00:24:13.184 --> 00:24:14.119
Sharp sword.

00:24:14.186 --> 00:24:15.086
Made good cuts.

00:24:15.153 --> 00:24:15.820
Well done.

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:16.421
 Thank you.

00:24:16.521 --> 00:24:17.956
Thank you.

00:24:18.023 --> 00:24:18.823
 All right, DJ.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:19.758
You ready?

00:24:19.825 --> 00:24:20.424
 Are you ready?

00:24:20.524 --> 00:24:21.259
That's a big one.

00:24:21.326 --> 00:24:24.162
 [laughs] I'm ready.

00:24:24.229 --> 00:24:27.833
[music playing]

00:24:41.479 --> 00:24:45.649
I can run my finger
along that edge.

00:24:45.750 --> 00:24:48.553
On the first cut, as soon
as I hit the dull part,

00:24:48.653 --> 00:24:50.822
it just starts
pushing stuff over.

00:24:50.922 --> 00:24:52.691
Did a good job
putting it together,

00:24:52.791 --> 00:24:55.160
but it's just not
sharp enough to cut.

00:24:58.229 --> 00:25:01.799
 Todd, DJ, you've both done
an incredible amount of work

00:25:01.899 --> 00:25:03.968
to bring these
massive swords back

00:25:04.035 --> 00:25:06.104
for our final round
of competition,

00:25:06.171 --> 00:25:08.640
but there can only be one
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:25:08.740 --> 00:25:10.175
And that champion is--

00:25:15.279 --> 00:25:16.714
Todd.

00:25:16.781 --> 00:25:19.717
Congratulations, you are the
new Forged in Fire Champion.

00:25:19.784 --> 00:25:23.554
DJ, unfortunately, your
sword didn't make the cut.

00:25:23.654 --> 00:25:25.790
Please surrender your blade.

00:25:25.857 --> 00:25:27.458
 My biggest regret
is I should have

00:25:27.525 --> 00:25:29.828
spent more time on the edge.

00:25:29.895 --> 00:25:30.862
I did my best.

00:25:30.928 --> 00:25:32.630
And I didn't want
to build something

00:25:32.731 --> 00:25:35.534
that was going to snap,
and I definitely did that.

00:25:38.503 --> 00:25:39.937
 Todd, congratulations.

00:25:40.004 --> 00:25:42.807
You are the new Forged
in Fire Champion,

00:25:42.874 --> 00:25:47.044
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:25:47.111 --> 00:25:47.812
Good job.

00:25:47.879 --> 00:25:48.379
 Thank you.

00:25:48.446 --> 00:25:49.280
[applause]

00:25:49.380 --> 00:25:50.581
Thank you, gentlemen.

00:25:50.648 --> 00:25:52.851
 Please present your
blade to the judges.

00:25:52.917 --> 00:25:54.252
TODD: I'm a little surprised.

00:25:54.319 --> 00:25:55.954
You know, it's still like
a surreal kind of thing.

00:25:56.054 --> 00:25:59.090
I've proven what I've come
to prove-- that I'm capable,

00:25:59.157 --> 00:26:00.392
that I'm still skilled.

00:26:00.492 --> 00:26:02.693
And I'm thrilled that I
was up to the challenge.

00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:04.228
I feel so good, I
don't know how to feel.

00:26:04.328 --> 00:26:05.196
[laughs]

00:26:05.263 --> 00:26:08.767
[music playing]

00:26:16.674 --> 00:26:19.243
WIL WILLIS: The bardiche.

00:26:19.343 --> 00:26:21.646
 Sweet.

00:26:21.713 --> 00:26:23.648
WIL WILLIS (VOICEOVER): Vicious
and menacing, the bardiche

00:26:23.714 --> 00:26:26.384
was a favorite of Eastern
European infantry soldiers

00:26:26.451 --> 00:26:28.786
during the 16th
and 17th centuries.

00:26:28.853 --> 00:26:30.888
Its large,
crescent-shaped ax head

00:26:30.988 --> 00:26:32.657
measured nearly two
feet at the edge

00:26:32.723 --> 00:26:34.726
and could cleave
through flesh and bone.

00:26:34.792 --> 00:26:36.995
Specialized soldiers,
called streltsy,

00:26:37.061 --> 00:26:39.664
would use the bardiche's
pole to balance their muskets

00:26:39.764 --> 00:26:42.400
for firing from a distance,
then switch to their ax

00:26:42.467 --> 00:26:43.802
during melee combat.

00:26:43.868 --> 00:26:45.636
Though rare in
American pop culture,

00:26:45.737 --> 00:26:47.071
you can experience
the bardiche's

00:26:47.171 --> 00:26:49.574
savagery on the virtual
battlefield of the game

00:26:49.674 --> 00:26:50.441
"Chivalry--

00:26:50.541 --> 00:26:51.442
Medieval Warfare."

00:26:51.509 --> 00:26:52.410
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:26:52.477 --> 00:26:54.679
This is the kill test.

00:26:54.745 --> 00:26:56.647
To find out how
lethal your weapon is,

00:26:56.748 --> 00:26:59.350
I will take your bardiche
and deliver lethal chops

00:26:59.417 --> 00:27:01.285
on this pig carcass.

00:27:01.352 --> 00:27:02.053
John, you're up first.

00:27:02.153 --> 00:27:02.654
You ready?

00:27:02.721 --> 00:27:03.421
 Let's do it.

00:27:03.488 --> 00:27:06.658
 Let's do this.

00:27:06.725 --> 00:27:10.295
[music playing]

00:27:11.529 --> 00:27:12.297
 Nice!

00:27:22.006 --> 00:27:23.008
Nice.

00:27:23.074 --> 00:27:25.076
Right on, brother.

00:27:25.143 --> 00:27:27.679
 All right, John, let's talk
about your bardiche here.

00:27:27.745 --> 00:27:29.681
I love the swells.

00:27:29.781 --> 00:27:31.082
By putting these
swells right there,

00:27:31.149 --> 00:27:34.152
it allows me to adjust my
hand and get a good grip

00:27:34.252 --> 00:27:36.321
every time I move it around.

00:27:36.421 --> 00:27:38.723
Your blade right
here is razor sharp.

00:27:38.823 --> 00:27:42.960
It cuts through spine,
bones, and thick flesh.

00:27:43.027 --> 00:27:46.364
Overall, sir, your
bardiche will KEAL.

00:27:46.430 --> 00:27:47.598
 I got something to show you.

00:27:47.665 --> 00:27:48.366
DOUG MARCAIDA: Sure.

00:27:48.433 --> 00:27:50.301
 A kill test?

00:27:50.401 --> 00:27:51.335
DOUG MARCAIDA: Oh, it will keal!

00:27:51.402 --> 00:27:53.771
[laughter] Good job.

00:27:53.872 --> 00:27:55.573
 I was hoping it'd KEAL,
because I had to do that--

00:27:55.673 --> 00:27:56.507
I did that.

00:27:56.574 --> 00:27:58.076
 Well, good job.

00:27:58.143 --> 00:27:59.077
All right, Michael.

00:27:59.177 --> 00:28:00.278
Your turn.
You got anything to show me?

00:28:00.345 --> 00:28:00.978
 No.

00:28:01.078 --> 00:28:01.679
 All right.

00:28:01.746 --> 00:28:02.446
You ready for this?

00:28:02.513 --> 00:28:03.447
 Yes, sir.

00:28:03.547 --> 00:28:04.214
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:28:04.315 --> 00:28:05.549
[music playing]

00:28:05.649 --> 00:28:08.085
 [breathes deeply]

00:28:08.186 --> 00:28:09.287
[music playing]

00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:10.088
Oh!

00:28:13.124 --> 00:28:13.892
Nice.

00:28:25.536 --> 00:28:27.706
[laughter]

00:28:33.511 --> 00:28:34.946
 All right, Michael.

00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:39.183
This is at least around 11
pounds, all forward weight.

00:28:39.250 --> 00:28:41.686
I waste so much
energy in recoiling

00:28:41.752 --> 00:28:43.755
that could be used in attack.

00:28:43.821 --> 00:28:47.124
But, overall, sir, your
bardiche will KEAL.

00:28:47.224 --> 00:28:48.259
 Yeah!

00:28:48.326 --> 00:28:49.127
Oh!

00:28:53.164 --> 00:28:54.899
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test--

00:28:54.965 --> 00:28:57.935
the stump thump and steer smash.

00:28:58.002 --> 00:29:00.205
To test the strength and
durability of your bardiches

00:29:00.271 --> 00:29:01.973
as well as their
overall construction,

00:29:02.039 --> 00:29:04.175
I'll be chopping
mercilessly into these logs

00:29:04.242 --> 00:29:06.477
and cleaving that
steer skull in half.

00:29:06.577 --> 00:29:08.812
Remember, this is all about
what happens to your bardiche

00:29:08.912 --> 00:29:10.882
and not what happens
to the wood and bone.

00:29:10.982 --> 00:29:11.983
John, you're up first.

00:29:12.050 --> 00:29:12.549
You ready?

00:29:12.650 --> 00:29:14.052
 Let's do it.

00:29:14.119 --> 00:29:17.522
[music playing]

00:29:24.595 --> 00:29:25.363
 Nice!

00:29:33.270 --> 00:29:34.572
Awesome.

00:29:34.672 --> 00:29:38.842
 Well, John, your bardiche,
it's got a nice weight to it.

00:29:38.909 --> 00:29:40.979
Not a huge fan of these
undulations in the

00:29:41.045 --> 00:29:45.449
handle because I want to be
able to move my hands around.

00:29:45.516 --> 00:29:46.450
I'm looking at the edge.

00:29:46.517 --> 00:29:47.685
It held up beautifully.

00:29:47.752 --> 00:29:49.487
Everything's still
straight and tight.

00:29:49.554 --> 00:29:50.221
Good job.

00:29:50.321 --> 00:29:51.389
 Thank you.

00:29:51.489 --> 00:29:52.423
 Michael, you're up next.

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:53.457
You ready?
- Oh, yeah.

00:29:53.524 --> 00:29:54.359
Hope you ate your Wheaties.

00:29:54.459 --> 00:29:55.192
[laughter]

00:29:55.259 --> 00:29:57.695
 All right.

00:29:57.762 --> 00:29:58.863
 Oh, boy.

00:29:58.930 --> 00:30:02.433
[music playing]

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:07.071
Oh.

00:30:11.876 --> 00:30:12.811
All right.

00:30:18.582 --> 00:30:20.018
[laughs]

00:30:24.321 --> 00:30:25.523
Whew.

00:30:25.590 --> 00:30:27.758
 Well, Michael,
first things first.

00:30:27.825 --> 00:30:29.327
This thing is heavy.

00:30:29.394 --> 00:30:30.127
 It's a beast.

00:30:30.227 --> 00:30:32.063
 But everything is still tight.

00:30:32.163 --> 00:30:34.665
There's no motion in it,
even after all of that

00:30:34.731 --> 00:30:36.734
chopping and smashing of skulls.

00:30:36.834 --> 00:30:38.469
The edge held up really well.

00:30:38.536 --> 00:30:39.637
So, well done.

00:30:39.704 --> 00:30:40.371
 That's awesome.

00:30:40.471 --> 00:30:41.739
Yeah.

00:30:41.806 --> 00:30:42.640
 Up next is the sharpness
test, and for that,

00:30:42.707 --> 00:30:44.976
I'll give you to David.

00:30:45.076 --> 00:30:46.176
 All right, gentlemen.

00:30:46.243 --> 00:30:47.779
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:30:47.879 --> 00:30:49.614
is all about what your
blades can do to the target.

00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:52.182
So I'm taking one shot right
down the middle trying to split

00:30:52.282 --> 00:30:54.518
those watermelon, put
half in one bucket,

00:30:54.585 --> 00:30:55.553
and half in the other.

00:30:55.653 --> 00:30:56.653
All right, John.
Are you ready?

00:30:56.754 --> 00:30:57.455
 Let's do it.

00:30:57.522 --> 00:30:58.356
 OK.

00:30:58.423 --> 00:31:01.960
[music playing]

00:31:02.493 --> 00:31:03.228
MICHAEL: Nice!

00:31:05.663 --> 00:31:06.898
 [laughs]

00:31:06.964 --> 00:31:07.765
 All right, John.

00:31:07.832 --> 00:31:08.766
It feels good.

00:31:08.866 --> 00:31:09.934
It's got a good balance to it.

00:31:10.001 --> 00:31:11.603
The shape of this
is really nice.

00:31:11.669 --> 00:31:13.337
The cutting edge,
curved like that,

00:31:13.437 --> 00:31:15.706
cut through the
watermelon beautifully.

00:31:15.772 --> 00:31:16.707
Sharp weapon.
Nicely done.

00:31:16.774 --> 00:31:17.775
 Thank you.
Thanks.

00:31:17.875 --> 00:31:18.809
 All right, Michael, you're up.

00:31:18.910 --> 00:31:19.844
Are you ready?

00:31:19.944 --> 00:31:20.644
- Bring out the beast.
- OK.

00:31:20.711 --> 00:31:21.411
[laughter]

00:31:21.512 --> 00:31:24.349
[music playing]

00:31:24.415 --> 00:31:26.384
 [breathes deeply]

00:31:28.719 --> 00:31:29.487
Oh-ho-ho.

00:31:34.425 --> 00:31:36.494
 Well, right off,
it's definitely sharp.

00:31:36.561 --> 00:31:37.961
But it weighs a ton.

00:31:38.061 --> 00:31:41.165
I like the design of
this, but build strong

00:31:41.265 --> 00:31:43.134
doesn't necessarily
mean build heavy.

00:31:45.669 --> 00:31:49.907
 John, Mike, you bladesmiths
have engaged in one of our most

00:31:50.007 --> 00:31:51.509
difficult competitions.

00:31:51.575 --> 00:31:55.112
However, only one of you can
be the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:31:55.179 --> 00:31:56.314
And that champion is--

00:32:01.619 --> 00:32:03.054
John.

00:32:03.154 --> 00:32:05.056
Congratulations, you're our
new Forged in Fire Champion.

00:32:05.123 --> 00:32:08.091
Mike, unfortunately, your
weapon didn't make the cut.

00:32:08.191 --> 00:32:11.462
Please surrender your weapon.

00:32:11.562 --> 00:32:13.664
MICHAEL: My experience here
was definitely a challenge.

00:32:13.764 --> 00:32:15.199
It pushed me to my limits.

00:32:15.300 --> 00:32:16.834
I learned a lot.

00:32:16.934 --> 00:32:19.036
I might not be the
Forged in Fire Champion,

00:32:19.137 --> 00:32:21.005
but I still feel like I'm
walking away a winner.

00:32:21.105 --> 00:32:22.506
 John, congratulations.

00:32:22.573 --> 00:32:24.976
You're the new Forged
in Fire Champion,

00:32:25.042 --> 00:32:27.645
and that is a title
that comes with a check.

00:32:27.712 --> 00:32:28.646
For how much?

00:32:28.713 --> 00:32:29.880
 10 grand.

00:32:29.980 --> 00:32:32.784
 Please present your
bardiche to the judges.

00:32:32.884 --> 00:32:35.486
JOHN: This is the most
mentally, physically,

00:32:35.553 --> 00:32:39.757
emotionally stressful time, but
also the best time in my life.

00:32:39.857 --> 00:32:40.691
Woo-hoo!

00:32:40.791 --> 00:32:41.959
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:32:42.059 --> 00:32:43.661
I'm super excited
to get home and tell

00:32:43.727 --> 00:32:44.795
my wife about the great news.

00:32:44.895 --> 00:32:46.197
And now the next
thing coming up,

00:32:46.264 --> 00:32:48.666
I'm going to be having
a baby boy, so, I mean,

00:32:48.733 --> 00:32:49.667
this is wonderful to hear.

00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:50.534
Thank God.

00:32:50.601 --> 00:32:54.105
[music playing]

